### Internal API examples (Ingestion Service)
#
# Consumer: Control Module. Run them from IntelliJ (green arrow next to each request) or
# copy them to curl. Start the service reading the books from sample_data/ (no internet):
#   Linux / Git Bash:    SAMPLE_DATA=sample_data java -jar ingestion-service/target/ingestion-service-1.0.0.jar
#   Windows PowerShell:  $env:SAMPLE_DATA="sample_data"; java -jar ingestion-service/target/ingestion-service-1.0.0.jar
# Without SAMPLE_DATA the books are downloaded from Project Gutenberg.
#
# The expected result of each request is written above it, for an empty datalake.
# The same checks run automatically in
# ingestion-service/src/test/java/com/zcj/ingestion/IngestionApiTest.java

@ingestion = http://localhost:7001

### Health check -> 200 {"service": "ingestion-service", "status": "running", ...}
GET {{ingestion}}/status

### Not ingested yet -> 200 {"book_id": 1342, "status": "not_available"}
GET {{ingestion}}/ingest/status/1342

### Ingest a book -> 200 {"book_id": 1342, "status": "downloaded",
###                       "path": "datalake/ranges/001000-001999/1342"}
POST {{ingestion}}/ingest/1342

### Same request again (idempotent) -> 200 with "status": "already_available", no new download
POST {{ingestion}}/ingest/1342

### Now available -> 200 {"book_id": 1342, "status": "available"}
GET {{ingestion}}/ingest/status/1342

### More books for the list
POST {{ingestion}}/ingest/11

### List -> 200 {"count": 2, "books": [11, 1342]}
GET {{ingestion}}/ingest/list

### Book that does not exist -> 404 {"error": "not_found", ...}  (permanent: do not retry)
POST {{ingestion}}/ingest/99999999

### Invalid id -> 400 {"error": "invalid_parameter", "message": "book_id must be an integer"}
POST {{ingestion}}/ingest/abc

### Invalid id -> 400 {"error": "invalid_parameter", "message": "book_id must be positive"}
GET {{ingestion}}/ingest/status/0
